# Crates that run while bytescape-helper is compiled, on all four release
# targets: the build dependencies of the helper and of every crate linked into
# it (its own workspace crates, libc, windows-sys, and the rest of its normal
# closure), and everything those depend on through normal or build edges.
# The list is pinned. `cargo xtask helper-deps` fails when that set contains any
# crate that is not named here, however deep in the tree it is and whichever of
# those crates asks for it.
#
# They are not in helper-deps.allow because nothing of them is linked into the
# program except what they write. Code that runs in the build of a program that
# runs with administrator rights is reviewed all the same, so every new entry
# needs a maintainer's explicit approval. Names only: a new version of a listed
# crate is a Cargo.lock change and is reviewed with it.

# The one direct build dependency. Windows only: compiles the icon, version
# information and application manifest (requireAdministrator) into
# bytescape-helper.exe. On Linux its build script does nothing.
embed-resource

# Under embed-resource: reads Cargo.toml-style resource settings.
toml
toml_datetime
toml_parser
toml_writer
serde_spanned
serde_core
winnow
indexmap
equivalent
hashbrown
foldhash

# Under embed-resource: finds the Windows resource compiler and the C
# toolchain.
cc
find-msvc-tools
shlex
jobserver
vswhom
vswhom-sys
winreg
rustc_version
semver

# Shared low-level crates.
cfg-if
libc
memchr
getrandom
rand_core
windows-sys
windows-link
